    "doc_id": "vdoc_1a65bd8f",
    "text": "How do India maintain relationship with Russia and USA both time as India is part of BRICS and  QUAD\n\nComprehensive decision-intelligence analysis on How do India maintain relationship with Russia and USA both time as India is part of BRICS and  QUAD based on 3 verified sources.\n\n# Navigating Multipolar Geopolitics: India\u2019s Strategic Autonomy Between BRICS and QUAD Blocs\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nIn the 21st century, India\u2019s foreign policy framework is characterized by a deliberate model of **Realism, Strategic Autonomy, and Multi-Alignment** [Source: Realism, Strategic Autonomy, and Multi-Alignment: Analyzing India\u2019s Engagement with QUAD and BRICS in a Multipolar World Order - IJFMR](https://www.ijfmr.com/research-paper.php?id=63289). Rejecting binary Cold War-style alliances, New Delhi engages with competing international architectures to secure national interests across distinct domains. \n\nThis approach is reflected in India's dual participation in **BRICS** (associated with Eurasian integration, economic multipolarity, and global governance reform) and the **Quadrilateral Security Dialogue (QUAD)** (focused on maritime security, supply chain resilience, and critical technology in the Indo-Pacific) [Source: Realism, Strategic Autonomy, and Multi-Alignment: Analyzing India\u2019s Engagement with QUAD and BRICS in a Multipolar World Order - IJFMR](https://www.ijfmr.com/research-paper.php?id=63289). \n\nThrough this matrix, India has rapidly scaled economic and defense-logistical ties with Russia\u2014expanding bilateral trade to **$68.7 billion in FY 2024\u201325** and ratifying the **Reciprocal Exchange of Logistics Agreement (RELOS)** in **December 2025** [Source: A Paradigm Shift in India-Russia Relations | Beyond the Horizon ISSG](https://behorizon.org/a-paradigm-sh",
