    "text": "BRICS 2026\n\nComprehensive decision-intelligence analysis on BRICS 2026 based on 2 verified sources.\n\n# BRICS\u202f2026: Building for Resilience, Innovation, Cooperation and Sustainability  \n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary  \n\nThe eighteenth BRICS summit (12\u201113\u202fSeptember\u202f2026, New\u202fDelhi, India) reaffirmed the bloc\u2019s strategic pivot toward **resilience, innovation, cooperation and sustainability**. Under India\u2019s chairmanship, BRICS expanded to **eleven full members**\u2014the original five plus Egypt, Ethiopia, Iran, Saudi\u202fArabia, the United Arab Emirates and Indonesia\u2014and formalised a **partner\u2011country tier** comprising ten states.  \n\nKey outcomes include:  \n\n| Outcome | Significance |\n|---------|--------------|\n| **Theme & Narrative** \u2013 \u201cBuilding for Resilience, Innovation, Cooperation and Sustainability\u201d | Signals a development\u2011centric agenda that blends geopolitical ambition with concrete economic and technological collaboration\u3010BRICS\u202f2026\u202fDeclaration\u3011 |\n| **Three\u2011Pillar Governance Model** \u2013 Political\u2011Security, Economic\u2011Financial, Cultural\u2011People\u2011to\u2011People | Provides a structured framework for integrating new members and partners while preserving decision\u2011making clarity\u3010BRICS\u202f2026\u202fDeclaration\u3011 |\n| **Cross\u2011Border Payment Framework Pilot** \u2013 Interlinking national payment systems for local\u2011currency settlement (no common BRICS currency) | Enhances financial interoperability, reduces reliance on the US dollar, and tests a scalable model for future trade settlement\u3010BRICS\u202f2026\u202fDeclaration\u3011 |\n| **Expansion Mechanics** \u2013 Soft\u2011accretion of Saudi\u202fArabia, formal accession of six new full members, and",
